Mogri / Primitive 94

Definition:
An irreducible held-open condition in which an important semantic object, intent, possibility, or partly inaccessible phenomenon remains available before a useful distinction is fixed.

Technical role:
Foundational conceptual or cognitive container; named zero-stage; not derivative from other CSP primitives; not an entity; not a cause.

Boundary:
This is a modelling role, not a claim that reality literally requires a Mogri container.

Origin route:
transmogrification -> mogrification -> mogri
